<article class="env-lemma" id="0GK0">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GK0">Lemma <span data-tag="0GK0">63.12.2</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to Y$ be a finite type separated morphism of schemes with $Y$ quasi-compact and quasi-separated. Let $K$ be an object of $D^+_{tors}(X_{\acute{e}tale}, \Lambda )$ or of $D(X_{\acute{e}tale}, \Lambda )$ in case $\Lambda $ is torsion. Then there is a canonical isomorphism </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  (Rf_!K)_{\overline{y}} \longrightarrow R\Gamma _ c(X_{\overline{y}}, K|_{X_{\overline{y}}})  \]
</div>
  <p> in $D(\Lambda )$ for any geometric point $\overline{y} : \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k) \to Y$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Immediate consequence of Lemma <a href="/tag/0F7L" data-tag="0F7L">63.9.4</a> and the definitions. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>